    "solution": "The nine-tile launch runway is ordinary ground: jump, land again, stop, or reset your takeoff there. Collect the tally on its right half, watch the patrols, then make a short leftward hop. Dash down-left back into the runway and jump left from that landing while the dash is still active; the dash has refilled, so this is an actual wavedash. Carry the low launch over the first patrol, then dash left through the second opening and grab the marked return wall. Climb through its upward crystal. Dash up and wallbounce right before the wall\u2019s upper thorns; take both rightward crystals and continue with the two up-right dashes onto the high gallery. The original grounded reverse-hyper entry remains a working alternative. Only the marked return wall arms on departure.",
    "nearestExisting": "F31 introduced the reverse launch toward an exit. F59 keeps its offset patrols and marked-wall aerial return, but its reusable runway now also supports an airborne wavedash setup. B59 teaches the one remaining spent surface: the return grip, not the takeoff floor.",
    "novelty": "Reusable wavedash runway through two patrol windows into a spent-wall wallbounce and aerial return.",
    "endingForgiveness": "The marked-wall wallbounce and three-crystal return remain the demanding finish. The takeoff runway can be reused without arming; the low overhead beam is 24px higher and begins 24px farther from the return wall.",
